<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador hits record banana exports in 1996.</title>
<headline>Ecuador hits record banana exports in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador banana exports grew 2.83 percent in 1996 to a record 3,842,442 tonnes, the official National Banana Program (PNB) said Thursday.</p>
<p>In 1995, Ecuador exported 3,736,533 tonnes of bananas.</p>
<p>PNB added that Ecuador earned $957.6 million on the 1996 banana exports, up from $846 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Ecuador is the world's top banana exporter.</p>
<p>The European Union was the largest buyer last year, importing 1.39 million tonnes worth $353.3 million, while the United States was the second, importing 875,557 tonnes for $222.3 million.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
